        "original_id": "a2903bc9-543d-58f9-9375-81c473fd4d9b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lion Gardiner\n- Places: Gardiners Island, Long Island, East Hampton, Suffolk County, New York\n- Roles: English settler, soldier\n\nFacts:\n- Lion Gardiner (1599–1663) was an early English settler and soldier in the New World.\n- Lion Gardiner founded the first English settlement in what later became New York on Long Island.\n- Gardiners Island is part of Lion Gardiner’s legacy and is held by his descendants.\n- Gardiners Island is a small island in the Town of East Hampton in eastern Suffolk County, New York.",
